To calculate the distance between two placemarks in Yandex Maps API, you can use the "getDistance" method from the "ymaps.coordSystem.geo" module, which calculates the distance between two geographical coordinates.

Here's a function that calculates the distance between two placemarks in Yandex Maps API:

```javascript
// Load Yandex Maps API
<script src="https://api-maps.yandex.ru/2.1/?apikey=YOUR_API_KEY&lang=en_US" type="text/javascript">
</script>

<script>
// Initialize the Yandex Maps API
ymaps.ready(init);

function init() {
  // Create a new map instance
  var myMap = new ymaps.Map('map', {
    center: [55.75, 37.62], // Map center coordinates
    zoom: 10 // Map zoom level
  });

  // Add placemarks
  var placemark1 = new ymaps.Placemark([55.75, 37.62]);
  var placemark2 = new ymaps.Placemark([55.85, 37.72]);

  // Add placemarks to the map
  myMap.geoObjects.add(placemark1);
  myMap.geoObjects.add(placemark2);

  // Calculate distance between the two placemarks
  var distance = getDistanceBetweenPlacemarks(placemark1, placemark2);
  console.log('Distance between placemarks: ' + distance + ' meters');
}

function getDistanceBetweenPlacemarks(placemark1, placemark2) {
  // Get coordinates of both placemarks
  var coords1 = placemark1.geometry.getCoordinates();
  var coords2 = placemark2.geometry.getCoordinates();

  // Calculate distance between coordinates using Yandex Maps API
  var distance = ymaps.coordSystem.geo.getDistance(coords1, coords2);

  return distance;
}
</script>

<!-- HTML container for the map -->
<div id="map" style="width: 100%; height: 400px"></div>
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your API key.

Make sure you include the Yandex Maps API script in your HTML and call the init() function when the API is ready.

This example creates a map, adds two placemarks with coordinates, and calculates the distance between them using the getDistanceBetweenPlacemarks function. The result is printed in the console in meters.

