When an object is being returned by value (as an instance), an implicit copy can be created. In the case of Vulkan objects like DescriptorSetLayouts, this can lead to issues with resource management. It's a better practice to use pointers or references to Vulkan objects and manage them explicitly. To solve the issue, you can modify the Renderer and Material classes to use pointers (or references) for the DescriptorSetLayouts.

