Upon reviewing the code again, I found that the invalid `VkDescriptorSetLayout` object is being caused due to the `Material::Initialize` method:

```cpp
this->descriptorSetLayout = *descriptorSetLayout;
this->samplerDescriptorSetLayout = *samplerDescriptorSetLayout;
```

These lines of the code are discarding the original `VkDescriptorSetLayout` objects and copying their contents to new objects, which are not initialized correctly.

To fix the issue, change the type of `descriptorSetLayout` and `samplerDescriptorSetLayout` in the `Material` class from `VkDescriptorSetLayout` to `VkDescriptorSetLayout*`:

```cpp
VkDescriptorSetLayout* descriptorSetLayout = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
VkDescriptorSetLayout* samplerDescriptorSetLayout = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
```

Then, update the `Material::Initialize` method to set the pointers instead of copying the contents:

```cpp
this->descriptorSetLayout = descriptorSetLayout;
this->samplerDescriptorSetLayout = samplerDescriptorSetLayout;
```

