After that, add the following `useEffect` hook:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
    if (isSelected !== null) {
      Animated.timing(bgColorAnimValue, {
        toValue: 1,
        duration: 200,
        useNativeDriver: false,
      }).start(() => {
        Animated.timing(bgColorAnimValue, {
          toValue: 0,
          duration: 200,
          useNativeDriver: false,
        }).start(() => {
          setIsSelected(null);
        });
      });
    }
  }, [isSelected]);
```

This will animate the background color of the selected item when it is clicked and reset the selected item after the animation finishes.

Also, you need to use `interpolateColor` instead of `interpolate` to interpolate between two colors. Try changing this line:

```
backgroundColor: bgColorAnimValue.interpolate({
  inputRange: [0, 1],
  outputRange: [
    item === isSelected ? colors.accent : 'white',
    'rgba(193, 199, 208, 0.3)', // set the end color here
  ],
}),
```

to this:

```
backgroundColor: bgColorAnimValue.interpolateColor({
  inputRange: [0, 1],
  outputColorRange: [
    item === isSelected ? colors.accent : 'white',
    'rgba(193, 199, 208, 0.3)',
  ],
}),
```

This should interpolate between the two colors correctly.

