You can use a disposable email detection API to check if an email is temporary or disposable. One such example is an API provided by Block Temporary Email (https://block-temporary-email.com). You can follow the following steps to check for disposable email addresses using C#:

1. Register for an API key on their website.

2. Install the 'RestSharp' NuGet package by running this command in Package Manager Console:
   ```
   Install-Package RestSharp
   ```

3. Create a method to check if an email is temporary or disposable with C# using the API:

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using RestSharp;
using Newtonsoft.Json.Linq;

namespace DisposableEmailChecker
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string apiKey = "your_api_key_here"; // Replace with your API key
            string emailToCheck = "test@example.com"; // The email you want to check

            bool isDisposable = IsDisposableEmail(apiKey, emailToCheck);

            if (isDisposable)
            {
                Debug.WriteLine("The email is temporary/disposable.");
            }
            else
            {
                Debug.WriteLine("The email is not temporary/disposable.");
            }
        }

        static bool IsDisposableEmail(string apiKey, string emailToCheck)
        {
            RestClient client = new RestClient("https://api.block-temporary-email.com/");
            RestRequest request = new RestRequest("check_email", Method.GET);

            request.AddParameter("email", emailToCheck);
            request.AddParameter("auth_key", apiKey);

            IRestResponse response = client.Execute(request);

            JObject jsonResponse = JObject.Parse(response.Content);
            bool isDisposable = (bool)jsonResponse["is_disposable"];

            return isDisposable;
        }
    }
}
```

Note: Replace `'your_api_key_here'` with the API key you obtained in Step 1. Similarly, you can replace the `emailToCheck` variable value with the email address you want to check.

When you run the program, it will output whether the email is temporary/disposable or not in the debugging console.

To create a C# software that can read Iranian license plates from images and write them into a text file, you'll need to follow these general steps:

1. Choose an Optical Character Recognition (OCR) library that supports the Persian or Farsi language
2. Set up the C# project
3. Load and preprocess the image
4. Perform OCR on the image using the selected library
5. Extract license plate text
6. Save the result to a text file

Here's an example using the Tesseract OCR library. First, install the Tesseract NuGet package to your C# project:

1. Install 'Tesseract' package via NuGet:

```sh
Install-Package Tesseract
Install-Package Tesseract.Text.Polyglot
```
2. Set up the C# project using the code below:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text;
using System.Drawing;
using System.IO;
using Tesseract;

namespace LicensePlateReader
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            var imagePath = @"path\to\input\image.jpg";
            var outputFile = @"path\to\output\text.txt";
            var tessdataFolder = @"path\to\tessdata"; // Download Persian (fas) trained data from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata

            var licensePlate = ReadLicensePlate(imagePath, tessdataFolder);

            if (licensePlate != null)
            {
                File.WriteAllText(outputFile, licensePlate);
                Console.WriteLine($"License plate number: {licensePlate}");
                Console.WriteLine($"Text file saved: \"{outputFile}\"");
            }
            else
            {
                Console.WriteLine("License plate not found.");
            }
        }

        static string ReadLicensePlate(string imagePath, string tessdataFolder)
        {
            using var engine = new TesseractEngine(tessdataFolder, "fas", EngineMode.Default);
            engine.DefaultPageSegMode = PageSegMode.SingleBlock;
            engine.SetVariable("tessedit_char_whitelist", "آابپتثجچحخدذرزژسشصضطظعغفقکگلمنوهی0123456789");

            using var img = Pix.LoadFromFile(imagePath);
            using var processedImg = img.Deskew(); // You may need more preprocessing techniques such as resizing or binarization

            using var page = engine.Process(processedImg);
            var text = page.GetText();
            var textWithoutNewLine = text.Replace("\n", "").Trim();

            return !string.IsNullOrEmpty(textWithoutNewLine) ? textWithoutNewLine : null;
        }
    }
}
```
3. Finally, run the project in your development environment and pass the path to the image you'd like to read the license plate from.

This example assumes that the image contains only the license plate. You might need to implement additional algorithms to detect and extract the license plate from a larger image.

Make sure you download the `fas.traineddata` file from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best and copy it to your `tessdata` folder. This will allow Tesseract to recognize the Persian language.

