```csharp
public class PersonComparer : IEqualityComparer<Person>
{
    public bool Equals(Person x, Person y)
    {
        if(x == null || y == null) return false;

        return x.Name == y.Name && x.Age == y.Age;
    }

    public int GetHashCode(Person obj)
    {
        return obj.Name.GetHashCode() + obj.Age.GetHashCode();
    }
}
```
In this example, `Person` is the class you want to compare and `PersonComparer` is a separate class that implements `IEqualityComparer<Person>`.

`Equals()` method checks if two objects are equal or not, and `GetHashCode()` method returns hashcode of the object. 

