The error you have encountered is typically caused when the region of interest (ROI) dimensions (width and height) or its position (x, y) exceed the boundaries of the image or have negative values. In your case, as you are trying to create training samples, this error could be caused by incorrect bounding box coordinates in your `output.txt` file.

To fix this issue, you can:

1. Double check the bounding box values in your `output.txt` file, and make sure none of the xmin, ymin, xmax, and ymax values are negative or outside the dimensions of the corresponding image. This can be done programmatically by loading the images and checking that the bounding box is within the image bounds.

```csharp
public bool ValidateBoundingBox(string imagePath, int xmin, int ymin, int xmax, int ymax)
{
    using var image = new Bitmap(imagePath);
    int width = image.Width;
    int height = image.Height;

    if (xmin < 0 || xmax >= width || ymin < 0 || ymax >= height)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Invalid bounding box for image {imagePath}: {xmin}, {ymin}, {xmax}, {ymax}");
        return false;
    }

    return true;
}
