This script creates a matrix-style animation on a canvas element. 

First, it sets up the canvas with the dimensions of the window and initializes some variables: 

```JavaScript
const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas');
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
const cols = canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
const rows = canvas.height = window.innerHeight;
const size = 10;
const chars = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789";
const charArr = chars.split("");
const matrix = [];
```

The script then creates a matrix using two nested for loops. Each element in the matrix represents a column in the canvas. 

```JavaScript
for (let i = 0; i < cols / size; i++) {
  matrix.push([]);
  for (let j = 0; j < rows / size; j++) {
    matrix[i].push(0);
  }
}
```

The `draw()` function is then created to render the animation. The first part of the function clears the canvas and sets the fill style to semi-transparent black. 

```JavaScript
function draw() {
  ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)";
  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cols, rows);
```

The script then sets the fill style to green and the font to Arial with the size defined earlier. It then loops through every element in the matrix and selects a random character from the array `charArr`. The character is then rendered on the canvas at the appropriate position. 

```JavaScript
ctx.fillStyle = "#0F0";
ctx.font = size + "px arial";
for (let i = 0; i < matrix.length; i++) {
  for (let j = 0; j < matrix[i].length; j++) {
    const char = charArr[Math.floor(Math.random() * charArr.length)];
    ctx.fillText(char, i * size, matrix[i][j] * size);
```

The script then checks if the current element in the matrix has moved past the bottom of the canvas. If it has, it resets the element to the top of the canvas with a probability of 0.025. 

```JavaScript
if (matrix[i][j] * size > rows && Math.random() > 0.975) {
  matrix[i][j] = 0;
}
matrix[i][j]++;
```

Finally, the script calls the `draw()` function every 50 milliseconds with the `setInterval()` function: 

```JavaScript
setInterval(draw, 50);
``` 

