To create a title in a Word document using C#, you need to specify the text you want to use as the title and add it to the document's header section. Here's some sample code to achieve this:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Office.Interop.Word;

// create a Word application object
Application wordApp = new Application();

// create a new document
Document doc = wordApp.Documents.Add();

// get the header section of the document
HeaderFooter header = doc.Sections[1].Headers[WdHeaderFooterIndex.wdHeaderFooterPrimary];

// add the title text to the header
Paragraph title = header.Range.Paragraphs.Add();
title.Range.Text = "My Title";
title.Range.Font.Name = "Arial";
title.Range.Font.Size = 20;
title.Range.ParagraphFormat.Alignment = WdParagraphAlignment.wdAlignParagraphCenter;

// save the document
doc.SaveAs("MyDoc.docx");
```

In this example, we create a new Word application object and a new document. We then retrieve the header section of the document and add a new paragraph to it. We set the text of the paragraph to "My Title" and format it using the Arial font, size 20, and centered alignment. Finally, we save the document to a file called "MyDoc.docx".

