To retrieve data from MongoDB with a condition that a particular field should be `true`, you can use the `$match` stage in the aggregation pipeline to filter the documents that match the condition.

Here's an example of how you can use the `$match` stage to filter documents where a specific field is `true`:

```csharp
var pipeline = PipelineDefinition<MyDataModel, MyResult>.Create(
    Pipeline.Match(Builders<MyDataModel>.Filter.Eq(x => x.MyField, true)),
    // Add more pipeline stages as needed
    Pipeline.Group(...),
    Pipeline.Project(...)
);

var results = await mongoCollection.AggregateAsync(pipeline).ToListAsync();
```

In this example, `MyDataModel` is the type of the documents in the MongoDB collection that you want to retrieve. `MyResult` is the type of the resulting object that you expect to get after running the aggregation pipeline.

The key part is the `$match` stage, which filters the documents based on the value of the `MyField` property. In this case, it checks if `MyField` is `true`.

