5. Finally, connect your Java backend to the frontend using a web framework such as JavaServer Faces, JavaServer Pages, or Spring Boot to render your web pages and process user input.

Please note that this outline is a starting point to help you build your tarot card reading website. The actual implementation will depend on the chosen web framework and the additional functionalities you may want to include. Additionally, you should ensure your Java application is running on a web server, such as Apache Tomcat, to host your website.

