To provide text suggestions when entering a city, you can implement an autocomplete feature using JavaScript and an existing list of city names. Here's what you can do to achieve this:

1. Find or create a JSON file containing the list of cities you want to support. Save it as `cities.json` inside your `db` folder.

2. Load this JSON file and parse it into a variable.

```js
const cities_data = fs.readFileSync("./db/cities.json");
const cities = JSON.parse(cities_data);
```

3. Create a new route in your Express app that will handle city suggestions requests from the client-side script.

```js
app.get("/city-suggestions", (req, res) => {
  const term = req.query.term;
  const suggestions = term
    ? cities.filter((city) => city.toLowerCase().startsWith(term.toLowerCase()))
    : cities;

  res.json(suggestions.slice(0, 10)); // Return the top 10 suggestions
});
```

4. Add a new script to your `search.ejs` file that will handle the autocomplete feature.

```html
<script>
  const locationInput = document.querySelector("#location");
  const suggestionList = document.createElement("ul");
  locationInput.parentNode.appendChild(suggestionList);

  locationInput.addEventListener("input", (event) => {
    const term = event.target.value;

    if (term.length < 3) {
      suggestionList.innerHTML = "";
      return;
    }

    fetch("/city-suggestions?term=" + encodeURIComponent(term))
      .then((response) => response.json())
      .then((suggestions) => {
        suggestionList.innerHTML = "";

        suggestions.forEach((suggestion) => {
          const listItem = document.createElement("li");
          listItem.textContent = suggestion;
          listItem.addEventListener("click", () => {
            locationInput.value = suggestion;
            suggestionList.innerHTML = "";
          });

          suggestionList.appendChild(listItem);
        });
      });
  });
</script>
```

This script creates a new unordered list below the location input field and populates it with the city suggestions returned from the server when the user types at least 3 characters. When a suggestion is clicked, it fills the location input with the selected suggestion and clears the suggestion list.

Don't forget to add the required CSS styles for the suggestion list to make it visually appealing.

