In Golang, you can create backend code that handles HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, OPTIONS, and HEAD. Here is an example of how to handle HTTP methods in Golang using the net/http package:

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "net/http"
)

func main() {
    http.HandleFunc("/", indexHandler)
    http.HandleFunc("/login", loginHandler)
    http.HandleFunc("/logout", logoutHandler)
    http.HandleFunc("/profile", profileHandler)

    fmt.Println("Listening on port 8080...")
    http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)
}

func indexHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    if r.Method != http.MethodGet {
        http.Error(w, "Method not allowed", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)
        return
    }

    // Handle GET request for /
}

func loginHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    if r.Method == http.MethodPost {
        // Handle POST request for /login
    } else {
        http.Error(w, "Method not allowed", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)
        return
    }
}

func logoutHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    if r.Method == http.MethodPost {
        // Handle POST request for /logout
    } else {
        http.Error(w, "Method not allowed", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)
        return
    }
}

func profileHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    switch r.Method {
    case http.MethodGet:
        // Handle GET request for /profile
    case http.MethodPut:
        // Handle PUT request for /profile
    case http.MethodDelete:
        // Handle DELETE request for /profile
    default:
        http.Error(w, "Method not allowed", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)
        return
    }
}
```

In this example, we define four handlers: indexHandler, loginHandler, logoutHandler, and profileHandler. Each handler handles a different HTTP route and method.

The indexHandler only handles GET requests and returns an HTTP error if any other method is used.

The loginHandler and logoutHandler only handle POST requests, and return an HTTP error if any other method is used.

The profileHandler handles GET, PUT, and DELETE requests using a switch statement to handle each method separately. If any other method is used, it returns an HTTP error.

Finally, we start the server and listen for incoming requests on port 8080.

Stripe integration will likely involve modifying `/assets/js/lesson-signup.js` and `/assets/js/account-update.js`.

For Milestone 1 (Signing up), you can add the following code to `/assets/js/lesson-signup.js`:

```javascript
// Set your publishable key
const stripe = Stripe('pk_test_1234567890');

// Handle form submission
const form = document.getElementById('checkout-form');
form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  const { error } = await stripe.redirectToCheckout({
    lineItems: [{ price: 'price_12345', quantity: 1 }],
    mode: 'payment',
    successUrl: 'https://example.com/success',
    cancelUrl: 'https://example.com/canceled',
    billingAddressCollection: 'auto',
  });
  if (error) {
    console.error(error);
  }
});
```

For Milestone 3 (Managing account info), you can add the following code to `/assets/js/account-update.js`:

```javascript
// Set your publishable key
const stripe = Stripe('pk_test_1234567890');

// Handle card element
const cardElement = document.getElementById('card-element');
const card = stripe.elements().create('card');
card.mount(cardElement);

// Handle form submission
const form = document.getElementById('account-form');
form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  const { error, paymentMethod } = await stripe.createPaymentMethod({
    type: 'card',
    card: card,
    billing_details: {
      name: form.name.value,
      email: form.email.value,
      phone: form.phone.value,
    },
  });
  if (error) {
    console.error(error);
  } else {
    // Send payment method ID to server for processing
    const response = await fetch('/process-payment', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        payment_method_id: paymentMethod.id,
      }),
    });
    const data = await response.json();
    // Handle response from server
    if (data.success) {
      window.location.href = '/account';
    } else {
      console.error(data.error);
    }
  }
});
``` 

Note that you will need to replace `'pk_test_1234567890'` with your own Stripe publishable key, and `'price_12345'` with the ID of the Stripe product/price you want to charge users for. Additionally, you will need to handle the server-side processing of the payment method ID in order to actually charge the user.

Writing a full tic-tac-toe game goes beyond the scope of what can be answered here, but I'll provide you with a structured starting point from which you can build the game.

```csharp
using System;

namespace TicTacToe
{
    class Program
    {
        static char[] board = { '0', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8' };
        static int player = 1;
        static int choice;
        static int flag = 0;

        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            do
            {
                Console.Clear();
                Console.WriteLine("Player 1: X and Player 2: O");
                Console.WriteLine("\n");
                if (player % 2 == 0)
                {
                    Console.WriteLine("Player 2 Turn");
                }
                else
                {
                    Console.WriteLine("Player 1 Turn");
                }
                Console.WriteLine("\n");
                DisplayBoard();

                try
                {
                    choice = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
                }
                catch
                {
                    Console.WriteLine("Invalid input. Please enter a valid number.");
                    Console.ReadKey();
                    continue;
                }

                if (choice < 0 || choice > 8 || board[choice] == 'X' || board[choice] == 'O')
                {
                    Console.WriteLine("Invalid input. Please choose an available cell.");
                    Console.ReadKey();
                    continue;
                }

                if (player % 2 == 0)
                {
                    board[choice] = 'O';
                }
                else
                {
                    board[choice] = 'X';
                }

                player++;
                flag = CheckWin();
            }
            while (flag != 1 && flag != -1);

            Console.Clear();
            DisplayBoard();

            if (flag == 1)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Player {0} has won", (player % 2) + 1);
            }
            else
            {
                Console.WriteLine("It's a draw");
            }
            Console.ReadLine();
        }

        private static void DisplayBoard()
        {
            Console.WriteLine("     |     |      ");
            Console.WriteLine("  {0}  |  {1}  |  {2}", board[0], board[1], board[2]);
            Console.WriteLine("_____|_____|_____ ");
