```typescript
import { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, ManyToOne } from 'typeorm';

@Entity()
export class Category {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id: number;

  @Column()
  name: string;

  @ManyToOne(() => Category, { nullable: true })
  parent: Category;
}
```

The `id` and `name` columns are defined with the `PrimaryGeneratedColumn` and `Column` decorators, respectively. The `parent` column is defined with the `ManyToOne` decorator, which specifies that a category can have many subcategories. The `nullable` option is set to `true` because a top-level category does not have a parent.

