To add Tailwind CSS to your Svelte project, follow these steps:

1. Install Tailwind as a dev dependency:

   ```
   npm install tailwindcss --save-dev
   ```

2. Initialize Tailwind by creating a `tailwind.config.js` file at the root of your project:

   ```
   npx tailwindcss init
   ```

3. Create a new Svelte component that will contain your styles. For example, create a file `src/styles/tailwind.css`:

   ```css
   @tailwind base;
   @tailwind components;
   @tailwind utilities;
   ```

4. Import the `tailwind.css` file into your `App.svelte` component:

   ```html
   <style>
     @import "./styles/tailwind.css";
   </style>
   ```

5. That's it! You can now use Tailwind CSS classes in your Svelte components.

Note: If you're using SvelteKit, you may need to configure PostCSS to process your CSS files. You can do this by creating a `postcss.config.cjs` file in the root of your project with the following contents:

```js
module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    require('tailwindcss'),
    require('autoprefixer')
  ]
}
```

To add Tailwind CSS to a Svelte project, follow these steps:

1. First, create a new Svelte project if you haven't already:

```
npx degit sveltejs/template svelte-tailwind
cd svelte-tailwind
```

2. Install the necessary dependencies:

```
npm install -D tailwindcss postcss postcss-load-config autoprefixer
```

3. Create a new configuration file `postcss.config.js` in the project root:

```js
// postcss.config.js
module.exports = {
  plugins: {
    tailwindcss: {},
    autoprefixer: {},
  },
}
```

4. Create a new file for your Tailwind CSS configuration, `tailwind.config.js`:

```
npx tailwindcss init
```

This creates a minimal `tailwind.config.js` file in your project root.

5. Import Tailwind CSS in your project:

Create a new CSS file e.g. `src/global.css`. Add the following:

```css
/* src/global.css */
@import 'tailwindcss/base';
@import 'tailwindcss/components';
@import 'tailwindcss/utilities';
```

6. Update the `src/main.js` file to import the `global.css` file:

```js
// src/main.js
import App from './App.svelte';
import './global.css';

const app = new App({
  target: document.body,
});

export default app;
```

7. Update the `rollup.config.js` to preprocess Tailwind CSS with PostCSS:

Here you'll need to install `rollup-plugin-postcss` dependency:

```
npm install -D rollup-plugin-postcss
```

Then update the `rollup.config.js`:

```js
// rollup.config.js
// ...
import postcss from 'rollup-plugin-postcss';

// ...
export default {
 // ...
 plugins: [
   svelte({
     // ...
   }),
   postcss({
     extract: true, // Extract CSS into a separate file
   }),
   // ...
 ],
 // ...
};
```

8. Run your Svelte project:

```
npm run dev
```

