Note that we've added the `$:` in front of `vehicleData = event.data.vehicleData;`. This is a reactive declaration, and it tells Svelte to re-run this line of code whenever any of its dependencies change (in this case, `event.data.vehicleData`). As a result, when the `vehicleData` is updated, the `RealEstateTable` component will be rerendered with the new data.

