This code opens two DWG files using the AutoCAD database API, reads the content of the files, and then compares the contents of the two databases using the `Objects.deepEquals()` method. If the two files are equal, the code will print "The two DWG files are equal." Otherwise, it will print "The two DWG files are not equal." Note that you will need to have the AutoCAD DWG processing API installed and referenced in your project for this code to work.

