        }
    }
    else
    {
        std::cerr << "Engine failed to initialize, exiting main loop." << std::endl;
    }
}
```

3. Add Delta Time Calculation:

Calculate the frame delta time for animation and physics calculations. The Delta Time is the time taken for one frame, i.e., the difference between the current time and the previous frame time.

```cpp
float lastFrameTime = 0.0f;
float currentFrameTime = static_cast<float>(glfwGetTime());
float deltaTime = currentFrameTime - lastFrameTime;
lastFrameTime = currentFrameTime;
```

4. Window resizing support:

Properly support window resizing by adding appropriate code for updating the related components like swapchain, viewport, and framebuffers when the window size is changed.

5. Make initialization functions in Engine class virtual:

To allow for better inheritance and extensibility, make the following functions virtual:

```cpp
virtual void Initialize();
virtual void Update(float deltaTime);
virtual void Render();
virtual void Shutdown();
```

By applying these changes, the Engine class can be more organized, error-resistant, and extensible.

