1. Use smart pointers for managing resource lifetimes: Instead of manually managing the lifetime of the Vulkan objects, you can use smart pointers specifically designed for Vulkan objects. One of the most popular libraries for this purpose is the "Vulkan-hpp" library, which is the official C++ header for Vulkan and provides RAII-style wrappers to simplify resource management.

Here's a modified version of "BufferUtils.h" using the Vulkan-hpp library:

