Here's an example function that takes in a `postID` and deletes the post from the database:

```javascript
const deletePost = (postID) => {
  const currentUserID = firebase.auth().currentUser.uid;
  firebase
    .database()
    .ref(`users/${currentUserID}/posts/${postID}`)
    .remove()
    .then(() => {
      console.log('Post deleted successfully!');
    })
    .catch((error) => {
      console.error('Error deleting post:', error);
    });
};
```

Here, `currentUserID` is the ID of the current authenticated user, `postID` is the ID of the post you want to delete, and `users/${currentUserID}/posts/${postID}` is the reference to the desired post data in the database. Calling `remove()` on this reference will delete the post data.

