To fix this, you can pass an extra option object to the `sheet_to_json()` method with the `raw: true` property. This option will preserve the original Excel formatting of the cell values, including any trailing ".00" decimal parts. Then, you can modify the `map()` function to check for cell values that are strings and end with ".00", and convert them to numbers using `parseFloat()` before rounding them to two decimal places.

