The current logic used for detecting activities relies on a simple threshold for acceleration and rotation from accelerometer and gyroscope data. It works for basic activity recognition but can be improved for higher accuracy. Here's an updated version of the `updateActivity()` function that uses different thresholds to better differentiate between activities and an average calculation for accelerometer and gyroscope data.

```java
private void updateActivity(float averageAcceleration, float averageRotation, int stepCount) {
    String activityText;

