To achieve this in Laravel Backpack, you can create a custom validation rule in your request. Here's how you can do it:

1/. In your app folder, create a new folder called "Rules" if it doesn't exist.

2/. Inside the "Rules" folder, create a new file called "AtLeastOneFileUploaded.php" and place the following code in it:

```php
<?php

namespace App\Rules;

use Illuminate\Contracts\Validation\Rule;

class AtLeastOneFileUploaded implements Rule
{
    /**
     * Determine if the validation rule passes.
     *
     * @param  string  $attribute
     * @param  mixed  $allFiles
     * @return bool
     */
    public function passes($attribute, $allFiles)
    {
        $filledFiles = 0;

        foreach ($allFiles as $fileKey => $file) {
            if (!empty($file)) {
                $filledFiles++;
            }
        }

        return $filledFiles > 0;
    }

    /**
     * Get the validation error message.
     *
     * @return string
     */
    public function message()
    {
        return 'At least one file must be uploaded.';
    }
}
```

3/. Now, go to your request file (usually located in `app\Http\Requests`). If you don't have one, you can create it using `php artisan make:request YourRequestName`.

4/. In your request file, use the custom rule we created earlier and apply it to all of your upload fields:

```php
use App\Rules\AtLeastOneFileUploaded;

// ...

public function rules()
{
    return [
        'field1' => ['sometimes', new AtLeastOneFileUploaded()],
        'field2' => ['sometimes', new AtLeastOneFileUploaded()],
        'field3' => ['sometimes', new AtLeastOneFileUploaded()],
        'field4' => ['sometimes', new AtLeastOneFileUploaded()],
        'field5' => ['sometimes', new AtLeastOneFileUploaded()],
    ];
}
```

Replace `field1, field2, field3, field4, and field5` with the names of your upload fields.

By doing this, the custom rule will check if at least one of the upload fields has a file, and if not, it will display an error message and prevent saving.

Note: The 'sometimes' attribute is added so that the rule will only be applied if any of the fields are present in the input data.

