To create a browser extension for Chrome, Opera, and Edge for www.blocksmc.com, follow these steps:

Step 1 - Create folder
Create a new folder on your computer for the project, to hold extension files.

Step 2 - manifest.json
Create a file called 'manifest.json' in the project folder and paste the following code:

```json
{
    "manifest_version": 2,
    "name": "Blocksmc Theme Switcher",
    "version": "1.0",
    "description": "Switch the theme of www.blocksmc.com from light to dark and vice versa.",
    "permissions": [
        "activeTab",
        "storage"
    ],
    "browser_action": {
        "default_icon": "icon.png",
        "default_popup": "popup.html"
    },
    "content_scripts": [
        {
            "matches": ["*://*.blocksmc.com/*"],
            "js": ["contentScript.js"],
            "run_at": "document_end"
        }
    ]
}
```

Step 3 - Create icon
Create a 48x48 pixel icon.png and save it in the project folder.

Step 4 - popup.html
Create a file called 'popup.html' in the project folder and paste the following code:

```html
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <head>
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        width: 200px;
        height: 100px;
    }
    .slider-label {
        display: block;
    }
    #theme-switcher {
        display: inline-block;
    }
    </style>
    <script src="popup.js"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <label class="slider-label">Dark</label>
    <label class="switch">
      <input type="checkbox" id="theme-switcher">
      <span class="slider"></span>
    </label>
  </body>
</html>
```

Step 5 - popup.js
Create a file called 'popup.js' in the project folder and paste the following code:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var checkbox = document.getElementById('theme-switcher');
    chrome.storage.sync.get('dark', function (data) {
        checkbox.checked = data.dark;
    });

  checkbox.addEventListener('change', function () {
        chrome.storage.sync.set({ dark: this.checked }, function () {
            chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, function (tabs) {
                chrome.tabs.reload(tabs[0].id);
            });
        });
    });
});
```

Step 6 - contentScript.js
Create a file called 'contentScript.js' in the project folder and paste the following code:

```javascript
chrome.storage.sync.get('dark', function (data) {
    var isDark = data.dark;
    var elements = document.querySelectorAll('*[style]');

    for (var i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
        var currentStyle = elements[i].getAttribute('style');
        if (isDark) {
            elements[i].setAttribute('style', currentStyle.replace('#008cd3', '#292b2c'));
        } else {
            elements[i].setAttribute('style', currentStyle.replace('#292b2c', '#008cd3'));
        }
    }
});
```

Step 7 - Package and install
To install the extension locally:

1. In Chrome, open the extensions page (chrome://extensions/).
2. Enable 'Developer mode'.
3. Click 'Load unpacked' and select the project folder.
4. In Opera and Edge, follow similar steps to load the extension.

With these steps completed, your extension will be ready to switch the theme of www.blocksmc.com based on the user's preference.

