You're correct that the method I suggested will still re-render the list and could potentially cause a performance issue. In this case, we can use a different approach.

Instead of updating the parent state on every change, you can update it when the form control loses focus (using the `onBlur` event) or when a radio button is clicked. This reduces the number of re-renders.

First, update the `handleContentChange` function:

```javascript
const handleContentChange = () => {
    props.setList((oldList) => {
        const newList = oldList.map((item) => (item === x ? { ...item, content: content } : item));
        return newList;
    });
};
