how to set the color of the form to green when check button is pressed?

You're right. As the `handleChange` updates the content of the block, it triggers a re-render of the block. In order to avoid this, you can set a new state variable, named `updateColor`, to determine when the component should update its color. 

Here's how to modify the `MyBlock` component:

1. Add a new state variable `updateColor`:

```javascript
const [updateColor, setUpdateColor] = useState(false);
```

2. Update the check button's onClick handler to set `updateColor` to true:

```javascript
<Button as='div' size="sm" variant="outline-success"
  onClick={(ev) => {
    ev.stopPropagation();
    handleChange();
    setUpdateColor(true); // Set updateColor to true when the button is clicked
}}>
  <i className="bi bi-check-lg"></i>
</Button>
```

3. Add a new `useEffect` hook to update the color based on the `updateColor` state:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  if (updateColor) {
    setColor("green-form");
    setUpdateColor(false); // Reset updateColor back to false after updating
  }
}, [updateColor]);
```

With these changes, the form's color should change to green when the check button is clicked, without causing any unnecessary re-renders.

