To write a React DOM code in Node.js, you would need to use a server-side rendering (SSR) approach. SSR allows you to render React components on the server and send the generated HTML to the client.

Here is an example of how you can set up a basic Node.js server with React DOM rendering:

1. Install the necessary dependencies by running the following command in your project directory:
   ```
