If the client makes 10 requests within the first 10 seconds, all the requests will be allowed to proceed and consume one token each from the bucket.

However, if the client tries to make additional requests within the next 50 seconds, the requests will be rate-limited because the token bucket will be empty. The rate limiter will prevent those requests from proceeding until new tokens are replenished at a rate of 10 tokens per minute.

